.TH "Method" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
stop \- stop STP service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]stp.stop()\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
Stp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to stop the STP service to which the current stp object is
connected.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
None
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, there is no return value.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
When the exception happens，use getLastErrMsg() to get the error message or use
getLastError() to get the error code.
For more details, refer to Troubleshooting.
.SH VERSION
.PP
v5.0 and above
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Stop the local STP service.
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> var stp = new Stp 
> stp.stop()
\f[]
.fi
